**Answer: ranking of FY2024 dividend payout ratios (GAAP basis, highest to lowest)**

1. Keurig Dr Pepper (KDP): 83.33%
2. Coca-Cola (KO): 78.86%
3. PepsiCo (PEP): 76.69%
4. Monster Beverage (MNST): 0.00% (pays no dividend)

**Method:** Payout ratio = FY2024 dividends per share ÷ FY2024 diluted GAAP EPS. I used per-share figures because they are the cleanest comparable inputs.

**Inputs and calculations**

- **Coca-Cola:** <cite index="31-3">For the full year, EPS declined slightly to $2.46, while comparable EPS (non-GAAP) grew 7% to $2.88.</cite> Dividends per share for 2024 were <cite index="6-1">$1.94</cite> (year-end table). Ratio = 1.94 / 2.46 = 78.86%.
- **PepsiCo:** <cite index="54-9">Diluted earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 6.95 compared to USD 6.56 a year ago.</cite> Dividends declared per share for 2024 were $5.33 (<cite index="18-1,18-2">Year: 2024. Payout ratio (%): 77.29.</cite> — the data provider's own ratio, which I did not use). Ratio = 5.33 / 6.95 = 76.69%.
- **Keurig Dr Pepper:** <cite index="38-3">GAAP net income decreased 33.9% to $1.4 billion, or $1.05 per diluted share</cite>. Dividends paid in 2024 totaled $0.875 per share (quarterly payments of $0.215, $0.215, $0.215 and $0.23; <cite index="24-5">2024 $0.875</cite>). Ratio = 0.875 / 1.05 = 83.33%.
- **Monster Beverage:** <cite index="57-2">We have not paid cash dividends to our stockholders since our inception and do not anticipate paying cash dividends in the foreseeable future.</cite> Ratio = 0%.

**Caveats**

- KDP's GAAP EPS was depressed by one-off items, including <cite index="40-6">$718 million in goodwill and other intangible impairments and an accrual for $225 million in upcoming distribution termination payments related to GHOST.</cite> On adjusted EPS of $1.92 (<cite index="39-4">Adjusted diluted EPS increased 7.8% to $1.92</cite>), KDP's ratio is 0.875 / 1.92 = 45.57%.
- On company-adjusted EPS, the ranking changes. KO: 1.94 / 2.88 = 67.36%. PEP: 5.33 / 8.16 = 65.32% (PepsiCo's <cite index="55-5">2024 core EPS of $8.16</cite>). KDP: 45.57%. Monster: 0%. Ranked on this basis: KO, then PEP, then KDP, then MNST.
- Dividends declared versus paid can differ slightly, so ratios computed from declared amounts may vary by a few tenths of a percent.
- The web results also contained later-dated payout figures (for example, 2025–2026 data). I excluded these because the analysis is set as of April 7, 2025.

**Sources:** Coca-Cola 2024 results release (Business Wire); Coca-Cola year-end dividend page; PepsiCo Q4 2024 earnings release (SEC Exhibit 99.1) and PepsiCo 2024 Annual Report (ARS); Fidelity PepsiCo dividend data; Keurig Dr Pepper Q4 2024 results release; Divvydiary KDP dividend history; Monster Beverage 2024 Form 10-K.

